    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1074">

                <pb facs="0936" n="924" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg924"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3831/255</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sparks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1018</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-23">September 23, 1940</date>.<lb/>[Received September
                        26.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    copy, with English translation, of the note from the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs, dated September 21, 1940, in which he expresses the desire of the
                    Haitian Government to conclude a new trade agreement with the United States on
                    the grounds that the present agreement<anchor n="64" xml:id="d1074-f1"/> and the
                    actual <pb facs="0937" n="925" xml:id="pg925"/> economic needs of the country
                    reveal that it would be particularly desirable to modify the existing agreement
                    as soon as possible. The Foreign Minister refers to Article 14 of the trade
                    agreement from which it may be interpreted that his present note is in the
                    nature of a notice to the American Government.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward J. Sparks</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d1074-a1.xml" xpointer="d1074-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1074-f1" n="64" xml:id="d1074-f1-content">
                <p>Signed at Washington, March 28, 1935. For correspondence concerning negotiations,
                    see <ref target="frus1935v04#pg_642"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1935, Vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">iv</hi>, pp.
                        642</ref> ff.; for text, see Department of State Executive Agreement Series
                    No. 78, or 49 Stat. (pt. 2) 3737.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
